id: pm-ts-starter-sdk-toon-codec
title: Use public SDK TOON codecs in generated backend projects
description: Replace generated standalone CLI direct codec dependency with public SDK codecs; preserve certified read-only receipts and document the supported host contract.
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ts-starter#197",sdk-adoption,template
created_at: "2026-11-06T18:46:27.416Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T10:16:35.348Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T09:02:39.777Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-08T00:45:54.000Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Generated imports and manifests agree on a supported SDK floor; real non-git tracker JSON/TOON round trips preserve representation and source state; regression tests fail on behavioral revert; document SDK codec pattern
release: 2026.11.10
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T18:46:39.844Z",codex-sol,"Scope: companion pm-cli-website-25wb and adoption audit S1. Inventory: backend-project.ts generates one direct production encode call and a direct codec manifest dependency; test/backend.test.ts directly decodes the generated CLI output. The package itself has no direct codec dependency. Replace these with public SDK codecs, retain read-only adapter policy and complete-list certification, and verify real non-git tracker output, inertness and generated SDK floor. Companion tracker remains read-only."
  "2026-11-06T18:51:00.094Z",codex-sol,"Public codec exports are present at exact generated floor 2026.10.17; peer range, dev pin and manifest remain aligned without a toolchain bump. Updated generated CLI and test imports to encodeToon/decodeToon from the public SDK, removed the generated direct codec dependency, and documented why application read-only/refusal/certification policy remains. Real non-git npm/Bun consumers and SDK harness pass 13/13 targeted tests. Disposable-copy behavioral reverts: restoring buildBackendProjectFiles alone fails host-owns-codec dependency contract; restoring cliSource alone fails generated build with TS2307 for the unsupported direct codec import. Fixed implementation rerun passes 13/13. Linked-test execution exposed inherited npm_config_allow_scripts causing EALLOWSCRIPTS in nested installs; consumer child environment now removes that setting and npm credential variables."
  "2026-11-06T19:05:49.100Z",codex-sol,"PR #197 is open at d2beea9. Targeted linked test rerun passes 13/13 with zero skips. Local strict health confirms history verification is healthy but reports inherited provenance advisory already tracked by pm-ts-starter-health-legacy-1027 and local extension-host version skew; no history rewrite or duplicate follow-up is needed. Full npm gate is running with a temporary home and disabled global/system Git configuration; Bun follows serially. CI jobs are queued for runners. CodeRabbit review is queued through the required pipeline; automatic skips, trial expiry and reviewer quotas are missing evidence, not approval."
  "2026-11-06T19:24:49.250Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and local acceptance complete: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/backend.test.ts passes 13/13 with zero skips, including the pm-linked run; npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and changelog check pass. Both isolated behavioral reverts fail and restored implementation passes. Per task instruction CI owns full npm and Bun release:check gates. An extra local npm full-gate attempt was stopped during unrelated compiler-cache tests after passing the generated consumer, crash-recovery and compiler-layout matrices; it is incomplete, not a pass. PR #197 first-head CI passed tracker health, committed-dist checks and CodeQL; full gates remain pending. CodeRabbit is still pending in the shared review queue, with no findings yet and no review approval inferred. External final-head receipts will be retained in the PR body. Existing local health advisories remain covered by pm-ts-starter-health-legacy-1027. No SDK gap or upstream issue was filed; linked npm install environment required clearing inherited allow-scripts as documented above."
  "2026-11-07T02:04:46.369Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched all review threads and comments (one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM60tmMd; no pagination gaps); latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Remote head is current and origin/main is an ancestor, so no merge is needed. Confirmed inherited private registry plus null user config can break public fixture installs. Preserve credential isolation required by the queue rules: explicitly select the public registry and isolate npm/Bun configuration for generated public-package consumers. Add behavioral regressions with synthetic hostile registry/configuration inputs; inspect the complete PR diff for similar paths. Keep all tracker history append-only."
  "2026-11-07T02:08:03.116Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed the review finding and applied a credential-free public-registry environment shared by generated npm/Bun installs. Synthetic inherited default/scoped registries, user config and Bun home config cannot divert fixture installs. Self-review exposed a second generated-consumer issue: fresh Bun installs may contain both nested SDK and hoisted codec versions; retain the SDK-owned copy while removing only the disposable top-level copy. Full-gate budget evidence: prior successful CI run 42279731772 took 62m44s npm + 64m05s Bun on Node 22, and 74m32s npm + 73m48s Bun on Node 26. Local full release gates exceed the requested approximately 60-minute budget; CI will certify them. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, build, docstring (14 files/53 declarations) and duplication (0%, 43 sources) pass at unchanged thresholds. Initial local health exposed global extension version skew; installing the exact CI project extension removes it. The inherited provenance advisory remains tracked by pm-ts-starter-health-legacy-1027; no history was repaired."
  "2026-11-07T02:12:06.168Z",codex-agent,"Review PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM60tmMd is fixed by credential-free public-registry isolation; authenticated host credentials are deliberately never read or forwarded. Self-review also fixed the fresh Bun nested/hoisted codec collision. Disposable-copy behavioral revert proofs with the fixed tests retained: (1) revert generatedProjectEnv to the original environment construction; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"generated consumers select the public registry\" test/backend.test.ts fails 1/1 (exit 1), selecting the synthetic unreachable inherited registry instead of the public registry. (2) revert only the codec relocation block; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"generated npm and Bun projects\" test/backend.test.ts fails 1/1 (exit 1) with ENOTEMPTY on an existing SDK-private codec. Restored complete backend suite passes 14/14, zero skips. The package worktree was never mutated for these proofs. Linked verification: node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-ts-starter-sdk-toon-codec --run --progress --timeout 900 passes 1/1 linked command, whose node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/backend.test.ts passes 14/14, zero skips. Additional isolated-Git validation: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/smoke.test.ts test/compatibility-floor.test.ts test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts test/package-metadata.test.ts test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts test/verify-release-changelog-date.test.ts passes 138/138, zero skips. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run build, npm run docstring (14 files/53 declarations), npm run duplication (0%, 43 sources), npm run audit:prod (0 vulnerabilities), npm run pack:dry-run, npm run verify:release-publish-attestation and npm run verify:release-changelog-date all pass at unchanged thresholds. Rebuilt committed dist has no drift. node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passes all gate-failing checks after installing the same project extension as CI; the single inherited provenance advisory remains unchanged and tracked separately. All changed history streams preserve existing HEAD and main prefixes. Whole PR source/test/docs diff self-reviewed; no additional finding or SDK gap remains. After claim release, regenerate and check the changelog, commit these records with the tests/docs and verify the final commit identity. Full npm/Bun release gates are left to fresh-head CI per the recorded 63-75 minute prior-gate timings. External check entrypoint: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/197/checks. No threads replied to or resolved, no merge or release."
  "2026-11-07T13:44:03.478Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round: both unresolved threads PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM60w3ol (Greptile) and PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM60xfIa (CodeRabbit) are valid and share one class: acceptance must execute against the package-manager-installed graph being certified, before replacement or reuse can hide its defects. Current branch and remote head agree; main is an ancestor and no merge is needed. Prior changes are preserved. Audit scope includes generated builds/contracts, built CLI JSON and TOON/refusals, SDK activation and non-git trackers, published SDK endpoints, packed npm/Bun consumers and CI install sequences. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Add a load-bearing adversarial matrix covering per-graph build, contract, CLI and SDK failures, prove failure on behavioral revert, then run focused gates and the full-gate budget policy unchanged."
  "2026-11-07T13:50:43.650Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed: generated consumers now have separate npm/Bun project roots and each runs install, build, contracts, built CLI JSON/TOON and refusals, SDK harness activation and certification-negative controls against its own installed graph. A nine-case adversarial lifecycle matrix (healthy plus every manager/phase failure) checks graph identity and every required phase. Additional same-class instances found and fixed: CI previously ran the Bun release gate before Bun installed its graph; move the fresh install between npm and Bun gates, preserve execution after npm failure, and require successful Bun install. Packed SDK consumers already had separate roots keyed by runtime and SDK bound, but CLI JSON/TOON/refusal checks were gated to npm/current; expand to all four installed graphs with a required 24-receipt matrix. Inspected published SDK provisioning, compiler fixtures, dependency-copy oracles, no-git checks, release install-only smoke and source SDK/CLI paths: no other cross-manager graph replacement before acceptance. Focused backend plus CI tests pass 25/25, zero skips; packed four-graph acceptance is running. Queue full-gate budget remains applicable: prior exact-head CI 42328089706 took 70m51s npm plus 70m25s Bun on Node 22, and 51m14s npm plus 50m31s Bun on Node 26 (101-141 minutes combined even on CI). Full npm/Bun release certification will therefore run in fresh-head CI rather than exceed the original approximately 60-minute host budget. No gate threshold changed."
  "2026-11-07T13:52:48.873Z",codex-agent,"Disposable-copy revert proofs completed for the reported graph class: restoring only verifyGeneratedConsumers to the prior shared-project npm-install/Bun-replace/npm-build ordering makes node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"consumer graph ownership\" test/backend.test.ts exit 1 with the graph-owner mismatch, while retaining all new tests. Restoring only the previous CI workflow ordering makes node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/ci-consumer-graphs.test.ts fail 1/1 (exit 1) because the Bun gate has no prior fresh graph install. Restoring both fixes and rerunning node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"consumer graph ownership|CI completes npm acceptance\" test/backend.test.ts test/ci-consumer-graphs.test.ts passes 11/11, zero skips. All mutations occurred in a disposable copy; no reviewed checkout mutation or history rewrite. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, rebuilt dist (no drift), documentation (14 files/53 declarations) and duplication (0%, 44 sources) pass."
  "2026-11-07T14:02:15.060Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance first attempt ended at the unchanged 120-second subprocess ceiling in the pre-existing Bun/current SDK invocation (spawnSync ETIMEDOUT), after earlier lanes completed. The command is unchanged by the ordering fix and overlapped another focused packed proof on this shared host; this is incomplete evidence, not a pass. Keep all thresholds/timeouts unchanged and retry packed acceptance serially after the other focused run finishes. Latest fixture tightening uses each installed SDK to initialize its own tracker and each runtime own minimum/current SDK roots for CLI checks; typecheck and lint still pass."
  "2026-11-07T14:09:55.385Z",codex-agent,"Additional packed-consumer behavioral revert proof is now load-bearing: in a disposable copy, restore only the old npm/current-only CLI guard while retaining the full receipt matrix. node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"packed npm and Bun consumers\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts fails 1/1 (exit 1) on npm/minimum because cli-json, cli-toon, refusal-json and refusal-toon receipts are missing. Per-lane assertions stop this omission immediately; the final independent 24-receipt matrix still guards all four runtime/bound combinations. The superseded earlier disposable proof was stopped and cleaned without claiming it passed. Restored packed acceptance is running serially at unchanged subprocess ceilings. Tracker fixtures are initialized by their installed SDK outside consumer compiler inputs. pm-linked CI regression passes 1/1; production audit reports zero vulnerabilities; release-workflow regressions pass 8/8, and release-publish/date verifiers plus pack dry-run pass."
  "2026-11-07T14:25:08.674Z",codex-agent,"Re-review acceptance complete for PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM60w3ol and PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM60xfIa: both valid findings share the installed-graph ownership rule and are fixed by separate generated npm/Bun consumers that each complete build, contracts, CLI JSON/TOON/refusals, SDK activation and negative controls on their own graph. Package-wide class fixes also make CI install a fresh Bun graph before its gate, preserve npm-failure semantics, and require packed CLI/SDK/no-git/refusal coverage for every npm/Bun minimum/current graph. No other instance remains in the audited package paths. Final focused commands: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/backend.test.ts test/ci-consumer-graphs.test.ts passes 25/25; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"packed npm and Bun consumers\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts passes 1/1 with all 24 required receipts (serial restored run, approximately 15 minutes); node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/release-workflow.test.ts passes 8/8. All have zero skips. node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-ts-starter-sdk-toon-codec --run --only-index 2 --progress passes 1/1 linked CI command. Three independent disposable-copy behavioral reverts fail specifically: shared npm/Bun graph ordering violates graph ownership; old CI ordering violates install-before-gate; old packed npm/current guard omits four first-lane CLI/refusal receipts. Restored graph/CI corpus passes 11/11 and restored packed matrix passes 1/1. Earlier parallel packed attempt hit the unchanged 120-second Bun/current subprocess timeout; serial retry passes the same stage and complete matrix without changing any timeout or threshold. Superseded disposable proof was stopped and cleaned without claiming a pass. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run build, npm run docstring (14 files/53 declarations), npm run duplication (0%, 44 sources), npm run audit:prod (zero vulnerabilities), npm run pack:dry-run and both release-publish/date verifiers pass. Rebuilt dist has no drift. Strict self-host health passes with the unchanged inherited provenance advisory; history remains append-only. Main remains an ancestor; no merge was needed. After releasing this claim, regenerate/check the changelog, commit these records with the fixes and verify identity/health on that commit. Full npm/Bun release gates run in fresh-head CI under the original approximately 60-minute host budget; prior successful pair took 101m45s-141m16s even on CI. Check entrypoint: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/197/checks. No review replies, thread resolutions, merge, release, SDK bump, or upstream issue filing."
  "2026-11-14T10:16:35.348Z",codex-sweep-1114,"Release-attribution correction: completed_at = 2026-11-08T00:45:54Z from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/197 (merge SHA b589a0e120283f3d5b4db208e86886c114866879); first containing release tag v2026.11.10, recorded release 2026.11.10."
